1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,960
<i>How do you feel about him?</i>

2
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:09,800
<i>He's pretty cute.</i>

3
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:10,880
<i>Nice smile.</i>

4
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:12,320
<i>Good at guitar.</i>

5
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:13,920
And he sings well.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,400
<i>But he's a bit too private.</i>

7
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,160
You can open your eyes now.

8
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:23,240
<i>Too scared to say I love you</i>

9
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:25,040
I can smell success.

10
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:26,720
Have you seen the post on X?

11
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:28,440
<i>What post?</i>

12
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,720
<i>Male idol with the initials P.T.</i>

13
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:33,160
<i>He's violent.</i>

14
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:35,920
<i>He once beat someone so badly</i>
<i>they ended up in the hospital.</i>

15
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:39,920
MISSALLSUNDAY: WAKE UP, EVERYONE.

16
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,560
<i>- P.T. is Phatee.</i>
<i>- I don't know him.</i>

17
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:43,320
<i>- P.T.? It has to be him.</i>
<i>- Unbelievable!</i>

18
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:45,040
<i>- He hurt someone.</i>
<i>- Unfollowed.</i>

19
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:46,520
<i>How disappointing.</i>

20
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:48,480
<i>I unfollowed him.</i>

21
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:51,240
<i>- I'm so disappointed.</i>
<i>- When will the label say something?</i>

22
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:53,080
I'll hold a press conference.

23
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:55,720
Phatee, just stick to this script.

24
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:59,280
Just tell them you didn't do it.

25
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:01,080
Let the whole thing blow over.

26
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:04,239
I can't deny it.

27
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,600
Because I really did it.

28
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:09,760
You? Hurt someone?

29
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,600
No way.

30
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:13,960
There must be a reason.

31
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:17,000
Whatever the reason,

32
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:20,160
I still ended up hurting someone.

33
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,320
I don't care whether you did it or not.

34
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:27,760
Just say these lines in front of everyone.

35
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:29,920
Even if I lie,

36
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:33,000
people will find out the truth someday.

37
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:36,080
If you want me to speak,

38
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:38,480
I'll only tell the truth.

39
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:41,280
But if you won't let me speak,

40
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:44,640
I'll take responsibility
by leaving the band.

41
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:48,200
Phatee.

42
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:49,840
Calm down.

43
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:52,520
We can take our time finding a solution.

44
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:58,080
This is it.

45
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,320
The solution.

46
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,680
Leaving the band is the best thing to do.

47
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:06,840
Don't you want to be an artist anymore?

48
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:09,680
If you don't follow the script,

49
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:11,840
your career will be over.

50
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,640
Are you really willing to
let that happen, Phatee?

51
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:22,560
Yes.

52
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:25,080
I really can't lie.

53
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:31,360
Phatee!

54
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:33,000
Phatee, wait!

55
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:34,480
Phatee, hold on!

56
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:35,640
Phatee, let's talk first.

57
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,560
What exactly happened?

58
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:40,320
Why did you hurt those people?

59
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,720
Phatee.

60
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:45,520
Can't you even tell me?

61
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:49,960
No.

62
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:53,840
So you're just giving up

63
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:57,040
and leaving me,
leaving everyone like this?

64
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:00,400
Phatee.

65
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,320
We've fought so hard to get this far.

66
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:06,480
We're about to release an album.

67
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,360
Soon, we'll have concerts.

68
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:11,520
Don't forget your dream.

69
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:15,600
If I stay in the band…

70
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:19,560
everyone else will suffer.

71
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:23,800
This is for the best.

72
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,400
Come on.

73
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:36,680
Kao will sort this out
for us anyway, right?

74
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:38,360
Just think of it this way.

75
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:40,080
This could make our band famous.

76
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:44,520
Any publicity is good publicity. Right?

77
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:47,440
I'm telling you,

78
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:49,240
this kind of fame will only ruin us.

79
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,440
Haven't you seen social media?

80
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:54,600
People are tearing Phatee apart.

81
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:56,400
It's even reached my DMs.

82
00:03:58,080 --> 00:04:00,960
So, has Phatee told you anything?

83
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:03,920
Nothing.

84
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,680
He won't answer any of my questions.

85
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:10,520
I hate to be this blunt…

86
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:16,399
but Phatee leaving the band

87
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:17,680
would be the best solution.

88
00:04:18,519 --> 00:04:20,240
Otherwise, our band is screwed.

89
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:22,960
We're screwed either way.

90
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:25,480
Without Phatee,

91
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:26,920
our band can't go on.

92
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:30,160
Kao only promotes those who can sell.

93
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:32,120
That's just Phatee and Ranne.

94
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:33,440
Without Phatee,

95
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,360
she'll only promote you.

96
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,440
No way.

97
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,240
How could she abandon you guys?

98
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,200
I won't let the band break up.

99
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:44,880
No matter what,

100
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:46,320
we have to stick together.

101
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,760
Here are your snacks.

102
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:07,680
Thank you.

103
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:09,200
Anything else?

104
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:10,920
Hey!

105
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,480
Don't you have practice today?

106
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:15,920
I've left the band.

107
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:19,200
Mimi.

108
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:20,560
Do you think he's okay?

109
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:22,560
Hey.

110
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:24,120
What a weird question.

111
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:26,000
How could he be okay?

112
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:27,840
He's getting so much hate.

113
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:30,840
Hey.

114
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:34,000
Hey, hey, hey!

115
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:43,880
Violent scumbag.

116
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:46,840
How dare he still sing at this place?

117
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,520
Please don't disturb the other customers.

118
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:53,160
What?

119
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:55,640
Does anyone want to hear this sadist sing?

120
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,720
If you've got guts, turn around and sing!

121
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:00,960
Hey, want some popcorn, buddy?

122
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:02,760
When you hurt other people,

123
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:05,760
- you weren't ashamed at all.
- Hey, calm down, guys.

124
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:07,840
Let's talk this through.

125
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:10,760
Would you like anything else?

126
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:12,360
No.

127
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,480
- Hey, hey, hey!
- Wait, wait, wait!

128
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:20,200
Where's the rush? Let's talk first.

129
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:22,000
- Don't you understand?
- Hey, let's talk, damn it!

130
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:23,560
Are you deaf?

131
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,080
Huh?

132
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:27,120
Hey!

133
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:31,080
You already went down?
I barely even tried.

134
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:34,720
I own this place.

135
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,960
I don't care

136
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,160
who you are.

137
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:40,040
But if you want to keep fighting,

138
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:41,800
take it outside.

139
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,680
This place is doomed

140
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:52,560
if you keep supporting that asshole.

141
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,480
Phatee.

142
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,880
Come upstairs and talk to me.

143
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:17,240
Anything you want to tell me, Phatee?

144
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:24,800
I'm no longer an artist.

145
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:28,040
I can't sing at the club either.

146
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:31,840
I probably can't pay you rent.

147
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,760
I think I should leave.

148
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:38,640
You're leaving?

149
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:42,039
You won't survive out there.

150
00:08:43,159 --> 00:08:44,800
When I give you a job,

151
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:46,200
learn to take it for a change.

152
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:51,960
You don't have to move out. Stay here.

153
00:08:58,360 --> 00:08:59,440
Stop.

154
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:09,600
Aren't you going downstairs to sing?

155
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:14,680
Yes.

156
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:16,680
Thank you.

157
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:44,480
<i>The label should take action.</i>

158
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:47,160
<i>I feel bad for</i>
<i>the other members in the band.</i>

159
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:49,680
<i>Won't you do anything?</i>

160
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:52,440
<i>Why keep him? Just fire him</i>

161
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:55,200
<i>and give someone</i>
<i>with actual talent a chance.</i>

162
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:58,000
<i>He almost beat someone to death,</i>
<i>yet he got off the hook.</i>

163
00:09:58,080 --> 00:10:01,080
<i>He must have connections.</i>
<i>That's why he got to debut at all.</i>

164
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:04,320
<i>I hope the label starts promoting</i>
<i>someone else instead.</i>

165
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:16,440
If it's money, I'd love to take it.

166
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:18,320
But if it's about Phatee,

167
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,280
I don't think I can.

168
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:21,920
<i>I understand.</i>

169
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:25,080
And I accept Phatee's decision.

170
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:28,840
But I won't let anyone spread fake news

171
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:30,560
to hurt others and get away with it.

172
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,920
I want to hire the Crows

173
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,080
to track down the Miss All Sunday account.

174
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:39,520
In that case,

175
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,640
The Crow Club is happy to help.

176
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:54,680
What is it, Linda?
Why did you call me here this late?

177
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:56,120
We've got a job.

178
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:59,640
What job? I'm going back
to Japan in two days.

179
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,200
That's why I called you here so urgently.

180
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:04,880
We need to find the owner of
the Miss All Sunday account before then.

181
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,520
Sunday what?

182
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,480
No way. I'm not looking for it.

183
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:11,440
It's an anti-Phatee account,

184
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:13,120
the one that made a post

185
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:14,640
saying Phatee beat someone up.

186
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:17,120
You should've led with that.

187
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:19,320
Let's go. What are you waiting for?

188
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:35,640
You've been searching since yesterday.

189
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:37,280
Still haven't found it, Vann?

190
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:38,600
Come on!

191
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:40,280
It's not as easy as it looks on TV.

192
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:41,560
It takes time.

193
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,800
If it weren't for Phatee,

194
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:47,120
I wouldn't sacrifice a romantic day
with my boyfriend to stare at a computer.

195
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:51,240
I could fly over with you.

196
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:54,200
So we can spend
a little more time together.

197
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:58,160
You two are always being lovey-dovey.

198
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,840
Don't be jealous of me.

199
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:03,560
You've got that writer now.

200
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:05,920
Wow!

201
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,240
A fierce tiger like Talay

202
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:08,920
got pounced on by his prey!

203
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:12,240
Prey is still prey, damn it!

204
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:14,240
Once I'm bored, I'll walk away.

205
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:15,360
Stay out of my business.

206
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:17,160
Worry about yourself.

207
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:26,520
What happens if you find that account?

208
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:29,040
I'll beat the crap out of them.

209
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:30,960
And then what?

210
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:32,800
Nothing will change anyway.

211
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:33,760
That's true.

212
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:37,440
But I won't let anyone keep hurting you.

213
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:40,200
Even if it doesn't solve anything,

214
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:42,800
they won't get to live in peace.

215
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:50,520
Hey.

216
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,240
Your future boyfriend

217
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:53,440
is pretty fierce.

218
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,440
Don't do anything to upset him.

219
00:12:56,520 --> 00:12:58,120
Otherwise, your life

220
00:12:58,800 --> 00:12:59,920
is over.

221
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:03,560
Found it!

222
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,760
I've located this account!

223
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:20,360
- Stop, stop!
- Right here.

224
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:23,200
- Here?
- I think this is it.

225
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:25,720
This is the location Vann sent.

226
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:52,320
What are you doing here, Ranne?

227
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:53,480
Come on in.

228
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,600
Why the hell did you do this?

229
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:01,680
What did I do?

230
00:14:03,040 --> 00:14:04,800
You're Miss All Sunday, aren't you?

231
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,240
The account that spread news about Phatee

232
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:09,800
and hurt our band.

233
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:11,680
You did it, didn't you?

234
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:13,320
What are you talking about?

235
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:17,160
I had someone trace
that account's IP address.

236
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:20,280
And it led straight to your house.

237
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:21,680
What am I supposed to think?

238
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:23,320
Are you crazy?

239
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,360
Why would I do that?

240
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:25,800
I've fought alongside you!

241
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:27,640
Then who else could it be?

242
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:41,280
I heard shouting, so I came down to see.

243
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:44,800
Tontoey.

244
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:45,960
Tontoey!

245
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:47,440
Tontoey!

246
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:49,240
Tontoey!

247
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:00,960
What are you doing?

248
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:12,600
Tontoey.

249
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:14,200
Show me your laptop.

250
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:16,120
Why?

251
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:18,920
The IP address is here.

252
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,800
And there are only two of us here.

253
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,160
Show me your laptop.

254
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:26,600
What? Are you playing a prank on me?

255
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:28,280
Tontoey, I'm not joking.

256
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:52,520
Tontoey!

257
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:53,800
Tontoey!

258
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:57,240
Tontoey.

259
00:15:57,760 --> 00:15:58,760
Tontoey.

260
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:04,560
Tontoey.

261
00:16:04,640 --> 00:16:05,680
Why did you do this?

262
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:07,160
It's my band.

263
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:09,200
Well, that's exactly why.

264
00:16:09,280 --> 00:16:10,480
I did this for you.

265
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,200
Don't you know

266
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:14,040
your label only promotes those two?

267
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:17,160
You practice like crazy,

268
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:19,880
yet people barely even know your name.

269
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,720
You're better than those two.

270
00:16:21,800 --> 00:16:23,360
You're way too talented

271
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,440
to be in a band
that only sells fanservice.

272
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:28,160
But it's my friends' band.

273
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:29,200
My band.

274
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:30,880
You have no right to do this.

275
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:32,840
